      "role": "scene",
      "canonicalText": "A young student remained in the house where she had been accused of poisoning two fellow students. She was about seventeen. The other women had fallen ill after leaving the house for an outing. One had said that she had been poisoned. The accusation had come back to the place where all three boarded.\n\nHer lawyer remembered the waiting that followed. The sick women had not recovered. She and the people supporting her waited for their condition to change. They hoped they would live.",
