    {
      "role": "dark_moment",
      "canonicalText": "The accusation remained against her while the two women lay ill. She was a Black student in a household shared with white students. Beyond the house, people were already arguing over whether she was guilty. Her lawyer's memory includes people judging her because of her color. He also remembers supporters who stood by her.\n\nTheir support could not settle the accusation. She had not yet been arrested. But she and her friends expected that the law would come for her. They had arranged for someone to defend her. The case was still coming.",
