    {
      "role": "response",
      "canonicalText": "She maintained that she was innocent. That is the response preserved in her lawyer's memory of the waiting. Her supporters maintained it with her. They also hoped and prayed for the two sick women to recover.\n\nHer own defense and their illness occupied the same stretch of waiting. There was no verdict to point to yet. She had counsel, and she had denied the accusation. She was still in the house.",
