    {
      "role": "struggle",
      "canonicalText": "Before any arrest, the danger became physical. Unknown people seized her and assaulted her near the house. Searchers found her in a field. The lawyer describes serious injuries and days confined to her room. When she could move about again, she needed crutches. Then came the arrest. Her lawyer asked for time because she could not yet attend court.\n\nHe obtained a delay, with a promise that she would appear when able. Her friends eventually carried her into the room used for the hearing. The prosecution presented its witnesses. The defense had found a problem with the claim that the women had been poisoned. No samples had been saved and tested. Still, the hearing continued.",
