    {
      "role": "turning_point",
      "canonicalText": "In the hearing room, the prosecution finished presenting its evidence. The court invited the defense to call its witnesses. Her lawyer asked for the case to be dismissed instead. He argued that the evidence did not establish the crime needed to hold her. In his account, the lawyers argued that question before the court.\n\nThen the case ended in her release. The same student who had been carried into court was carried out again. This time her fellow students took her home after she had been cleared in the poisoning case. The charge no longer held her there.",
